Negative control for client-emails-filter-sort.spec.ts (AC7).

Makes the recorded-corpus collection handler ignore the request's own params and
serve all three rows unconditionally — design §7's named hazard ("the shipped
`installEmailsListHandler` ignores `request.url` entirely, so any filter/sort
assertion behind it is vacuously green") made executable. Under it, a filter
that never reached the wire would still leave the rendered rows intact, so the
narrowing and reordering assertions must go RED.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Proven RED 2026-08-08
(`pnpm exec playwright test --config=playwright.config.ts --project lane`):
  x a filter narrows the rendered rows through a real re-query
      -> toHaveCount failed: Expected 2, Received 3
  x a sort reorders the rendered rows and ships the order param
      -> toHaveText failed (rendered order unchanged)
  x the filter and the sort survive a reload
      -> toHaveCount failed: Expected 2, Received 3
  v a sort field the module does not offer never reaches the wire
      (stays green by design — a pure wire assertion the served rows cannot mask)
  3 failed | 1 passed

